 "title": "FN 406 single-phase PCB EMC filter, 0.5 to 8.4 A, 250 VAC, standard and medical (B) versions",
 "source": {
  "revision": "29. Jan 2025",
  "pages": 4
 },
 "summary": "A single-phase mains EMC filter in an aluminium can with five through-hole pins for soldering to a board. Inside are an X capacitor and a bleed resistor across the line, a choke with one winding in each conductor on a shared core and, in the standard version, a pair of Y capacitors to protective earth on the load side. Five current ratings from 0.5 to 8.4 A share one case; the B versions leave out the Y capacitors, cutting the earth leakage to 2 µA for medical equipment. FN406-6-02 is the 6 A standard version.",
