 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Internal circuit",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Between the line pins P and N sits the X capacitor Cx, with the discharge resistor R in parallel. Next comes the choke: one winding L in each conductor on a shared core. On the load side two Y capacitors Cy run from P' and from N' to a common node on PE. The B versions have no Y capacitors."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Standard and medical versions",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "At each current rating both versions have the same inductance, Cx, R, connections and weight. The standard version carries 2.2 nF Y capacitors and leaks up to 373 µA at 230 VAC/50 Hz; the B (medical) version has none and leaks up to 2 µA. The B version is hipot-tested phase to earth at 2500 VAC for 2 s, the standard at 2000 VAC."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current ratings and inductance",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Inductance falls as the current rating rises: 24 mH at 0.5 A, 12 mH at 1 A, 2.5 mH at 3 A, 0.78 mH at 6 A and 0.3 mH at 8.4 A. The ratings hold at 40 °C ambient; the 25 °C ratings are 0.6, 1.2, 3.6, 6.9 and 9.6 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Attenuation",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Attenuation is measured per CISPR 17 with four source/load impedance pairs: A, 50 Ω/50 Ω symmetrical; B, 50 Ω/50 Ω asymmetrical; C, 0.1 Ω/100 Ω and D, 100 Ω/0.1 Ω, both symmetrical. The 0.5, 1 and 3 A types share one set of typical curves; the 6 A and 8.4 A types each have their own."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and approvals",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The case is aluminium and the design meets UL 94 V-0 flammability. The design follows UL 1283, CSA 22.2 No. 8 1986 and IEC/EN 60939; the part carries UL, CSA and ENEC marks and is RoHS compliant. Climatic category 25/100/21. MTBF to Mil-HB-217F exceeds 1,900,000 h at 40 °C and 230 V. Weight is 36 g."
  }
